      "review_notes": "The law is the verified reinforced urn with common-denominator shapes a*d, c*b and reinforcement b*d. Its inherited rising-product word masses give the beta-binomial characterization. The CTE proof checks rational domains, clears denominators, and applies the verified urn specification. This is a derived named-law specialization; its mathematical argument is inherited rather than duplicated. Independent callers cover arbitrary resource framing, zero trials, infinite credits, and one trial with shapes 2/3 and 5/7, whose success mass is 14/29."
