      "review_notes": "The target is the existing canonical finite uniform law. A prefix followed by a binary suffix gives one uniform integer block; the central expectation identity partitions that block into two equal halves. Arbitrary ENNReal credits are retained throughout, with no cancellation or real-valued conversion of credits. Symbolic execution is finite induction, one fair integer bit, and the recursive call; binder normalization is isolated from the interval mathematics. Independent callers cover the empty word, arbitrary bit counts, infinite credits, and preservation of an arbitrary caller resource."
